.TH SESSLINT-CHECK 1 "" "SessLint 0.4.1" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-check \- [read\-only] Check session artifacts (files, directories, or agent session roots).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint check [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-\-profile PROFILE] [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-\-latest] [\-\-include\-archived] [\-\-follow\-symlinks] [\-\-max\-files MAX_FILES] [\-\-max\-bytes MAX_BYTES] [\-\-json] [\-f | \-\-format {human,json,sarif,html}] [\-o | \-\-output FILE] [\-\-progress\-json] [\-\-no\-progress] [\-\-top N] [\-\-group\-by {code,none}] [\-\-jobs N] [\-\-incremental] [\-\-cache\-dir DIR] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}] [\-\-no\-color] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] [\-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN] [\-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN] [\-\-skip\-undetected] [\-\-fail\-on {error,warning}] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-select CODES] [\-\-ignore CODES] [\-\-baseline PATH] [\-\-write\-baseline PATH] [\-\-exclude GLOB] [\-\-ext EXT] [\-\-include\-content] [\-\-seal LEDGER] [\-\-seal\-no\-path] [\-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX] [\-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES] [\-\-timestamp\-skew\-ms TIMESTAMP_SKEW_MS] [\-\-fail\-on\-unsupported] [\-\-max\-findings\-per\-code MAX_FINDINGS_PER_CODE] [\-\-newest N] [\-\-since YYYY\-MM\-DD] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Check session artifacts for structural defects, causal breaks, and schema violations. Positional targets may be files, directories (scanned recursively), or '\-' to read one session file from stdin. 'scan' is an alias for this command.
\&'sesslint scan' is an alias for 'sesslint check'.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to session file(s) (.json or .jsonl) or directories. Multiple paths produce one aggregated scan report. '\-' reads one session artifact from stdin (max 100 MB). Omit PATH only when using \-\-agent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter (default: auto) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents.
.TP
.B \-\-profile PROFILE
Replay validation profile (default: neutral)
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Scan well\-known session roots for an agent runtime ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects or ~/.claude/projects; $CODEX_HOME/sessions or ~/.codex/sessions). Explicit PATH overrides. Choices: claude, codex, all.
.TP
.B \-\-latest
Check only the newest primary ledger for \-\-agent claude|codex
.TP
.B \-\-include\-archived
Include Codex archived_sessions during agent discovery
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-symlinks
[lossy: follows links] Follow directory symlinks during recursive scanning
.TP
.B \-\-max\-files MAX_FILES
Maximum number of files to inspect during recursive scan (default: 10000)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-bytes MAX_BYTES
Maximum cumulative bytes to read during recursive scan (default: 1GB)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output check report as a single canonical JSON document to stdout
.TP
.B \-f {human,json,sarif,html}, \-\-format {human,json,sarif,html}
Output format (default: human; \-\-json is equivalent to 'json') Choices: human, json, sarif, html.
.TP
.B \-o FILE, \-\-output FILE
Write the report to FILE instead of stdout (existing report files are overwritten atomically)
.TP
.B \-\-progress\-json
Emit NDJSON progress events to stderr (stdout stays the result channel)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-progress
Disable interactive progress output on stderr
.TP
.B \-\-top N
Show up to N worst files in the report summary (default: 10; 0 disables the worst\-files view) Default: 10.
.TP
.B \-\-group\-by {code,none}
Summary grouping: 'code' aggregates findings by rule code (default), 'none' disables Choices: code, none. Default: code.
.TP
.B \-\-jobs N
Parallel worker processes for per\-file analysis (default: 1 = sequential; 'auto' or 0 = CPU count). Report output is identical for any N; only wall time changes. Ignored for single\-file input. Default: 1.
.TP
.B \-\-incremental
Reuse cached per\-file results when content is provably unchanged (sqlite cache; findings/verdicts identical, hits marked 'cache: hit')
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir DIR
Override the incremental cache directory (default: SESSLINT_CACHE_DIR or platform cache location)
.TP
.B \-\-color {auto,always,never}
Control colored terminal output (default: auto) Choices: auto, always, never.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color styling
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.TP
.B \-\-confidence\-min CONFIDENCE_MIN
Format auto\-detection minimum confidence threshold
.TP
.B \-\-margin\-min MARGIN_MIN
Format auto\-detection minimum margin threshold
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-undetected
Classify files whose format cannot be detected as skipped instead of invalid (useful for pre\-commit hooks and mixed\-content trees)
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on {error,warning}
Minimum finding severity that fails the command (default: error) Choices: error, warning.
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
Explicit config file path (overrides [tool.sesslint] discovery)
.TP
.B \-\-select CODES
Comma\-separated rule codes to run exclusively (e.g. SL101,SL102)
.TP
.B \-\-ignore CODES
Comma\-separated rule codes to skip (e.g. SL101,SL102)
.TP
.B \-\-baseline PATH
Suppress findings whose fingerprints are recorded in baseline file
.TP
.B \-\-write\-baseline PATH
Write the current finding fingerprints as a new baseline file
.TP
.B \-\-exclude GLOB
Skip files/dirs whose name or root\-relative path matches GLOB (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-ext EXT
Only inspect files with these extensions during directory walks (repeatable)
.TP
.B \-\-include\-content
Embed raw transcript content in reports (warning: emits raw sensitive data)
.TP
.B \-\-seal LEDGER
Append a tamper\-evident seal line to LEDGER (append\-only hash\-chained verdict record; 'sesslint seal \-\-verify' re\-checks it)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-no\-path
Omit the artifact path from the seal line (multi\-machine ledgers)
.TP
.B \-\-seal\-genesis\-of HEX
Bind a new ledger's first line to a prior ledger's last entry hash (ledger rotation)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES
Skip files above this byte limit (default: 104857600)
.TP
.B \-\-timestamp\-skew\-ms TIMESTAMP_SKEW_MS
Allowed backwards timestamp skew in milliseconds (default: 2000)
.TP
.B \-\-fail\-on\-unsupported
Exit 1 for unsupported formats as well as invalid inputs
.TP
.B \-\-max\-findings\-per\-code MAX_FINDINGS_PER_CODE
Maximum displayed samples per code per file (default: 20)
.TP
.B \-\-newest N
Inspect the N most recently modified session files
.TP
.B \-\-since YYYY\-MM\-DD
Inspect files modified on/after this absolute UTC date
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success — clean check, or repair executed, validated, and manifested.
.TP
.B 1
Finding / refusal — diagnostic errors found, repair plan blocked, or
execution refused (TOCTOU, SL203).
.TP
.B 2
Operational error — CLI syntax error, file not found, permission denied,
or live-DB path refusal.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-completion(1), sesslint\-diff(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

